==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]].
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Professor A.]] spawns.
**2 [[Bore]]s spawn, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Bring [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island]], [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] and [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] as your main [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red Cats]] and make sure to lure the Bores to your base. Once the Bores have been cleared, you should still continue to lure until the battle nears its end, as pushing far enough may trigger the Relic Doge Base.

Resist Curse [[Talents]] can be helpful for nullifying the Relic Doge Base' effect if you are not trying to lure, and if you perma-[[Freeze|freeze]] Bore with an aforementioned iCat then you can start stacking [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance Cats]] like [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]] or [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]] in order to defeat Professor A. and Dark Emperor Nyandam. It is wise to farm money off of the B.B.Bunnies with a [[Money Up]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and/or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]. [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Luxury Bath Cat]] is also a decent damage dealer if you need one.

If you haven't brought anything to outrange Professor A. and both Bores are dead, spam Roe Cats and Manic Island Cats, and time Bullet Train Cat and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] for damage until you win. If your money is getting low, then stop spamming Manic Islands for a bit and continue when it is at a stable level.

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Theatre of Fear]] stages, Spiralling Ring is a horror movie reference, in this case to ''[[wikipedia:Ring (film)|Ring]]'' and its sequel ''[[wikipedia:Spiral (1998 film)|Spiral]]''.
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], the stage width was set to 4,100. The change was made because of a bug in how [[:Category:Animated Enemy Bases|Animated Bases]] spawn when not set as bosses.

